---
import SiteLayout from "@/layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Install Agent Toolkit or get Veasel Code"
  description="Agent Toolkit is a portable CLI and capability ecosystem. Its legacy Desktop is retired; Veasel Code is the supported graphical coding application."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Product migration</p>
      <h1>Agent Toolkit Desktop is retired.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Agent Toolkit continues as a portable CLI and capability ecosystem. For
        a graphical coding application with Focus, World, and a shared TUI
        backend, use Veasel Code.
      </p>
      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="button button--sun" href="https://www.veasel.dev/downloads/">
          Download Veasel Code{" "}
          <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">
            ↗
          </span>
        </a>
        <a class="button button--outline" href="/docs/installation/">
          Install Agent Toolkit CLI
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section--deep" style="padding-top: 8px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p class="section-kicker">Portable capability toolkit</p>
        <h2>Install the CLI for your coding tools.</h2>
        <p>
          The CLI discovers supported tools and previews target paths before it
          installs capabilities. Review the preview and preserve files you own.
          Exact support depends on each tool and capability.
        </p>
      </div>
      <pre class="cli-command"><code>uv tool install agent-toolkit-cli</code></pre>
      <p style="color: var(--muted)">
        Other supported channels and verification steps are in the
        <a href="/docs/installation/">installation guide</a>. See
        <a href="/docs/compatibility/">compatibility</a> for target-specific
        support.
      </p>
      <div class="migration-note">
        <strong>Moving from the legacy Desktop?</strong>
        <p>
          Existing installations and their data remain on your device. Veasel
          does not automatically import legacy Toolkit Desktop data. Back up
          your profile before removing an old installation, and use the
          migration notes before moving any configuration.
        </p>
        <a href="https://github.com/ulises-jeremias/agent-toolkit/blob/main/docs/INSTALLATION.md">
          Read the migration and installation notes ↗
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
